PART 3: INSTALLING BOOTSTRAP IN REACT
================================================================================

STEP 1: INSTALL BOOTSTRAP
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Run:

npm install bootstrap


Verify:

npm list bootstrap


WHAT THIS DOES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

• Downloads the Bootstrap npm package

• Adds the package to node_modules

• Adds Bootstrap to package.json dependencies

• Makes Bootstrap files available for import


================================================================================
STEP 2: IMPORT BOOTSTRAP CSS IN main.jsx
================================================================================

File:

src/main.jsx


import React from 'react'

import ReactDOM
  from 'react-dom/client'

import App
  from './App.jsx'


// Bootstrap CSS

import 'bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css'


// Application/global CSS
// Imported after Bootstrap so custom rules can participate later
// in the cascade where specificity is otherwise comparable.

import './index.css'


ReactDOM.createRoot(
  document.getElementById('root')
).render(

  <React.StrictMode>

    <App />

  </React.StrictMode>

)


IMPORT EXPLANATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

+------------------------------------------+----------------------------------+
| CODE                                     | PURPOSE                          |
+------------------------------------------+----------------------------------+
| bootstrap.min.css                        | Loads Bootstrap CSS              |
| index.css                                | Loads custom global CSS          |
| ReactDOM.createRoot(...)                 | Creates React root               |
| document.getElementById('root')          | Finds application root           |
| <React.StrictMode>                       | Development checks               |
| <App />                                  | Renders main application         |
+------------------------------------------+----------------------------------+


IMPORTANT: BOOTSTRAP CSS VS JAVASCRIPT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Many Bootstrap features need ONLY CSS.

Examples:

• Grid
• Buttons
• Cards
• Spacing utilities
• Typography utilities
• Colors
• Spinners


Some interactive Bootstrap components require Bootstrap JavaScript.

Examples include:

• Dismissible alerts
• Dropdowns
• Modals
• Collapse
• Tooltips
• Popovers


If Bootstrap JavaScript behavior is required, the application must include
the appropriate Bootstrap JavaScript setup.

For example:

import 'bootstrap/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js'


Do NOT import Bootstrap JavaScript merely for simple CSS-only components
if the application doesn't need it.


