PART 4: BOOTSTRAP GRID SYSTEM
================================================================================

BOOTSTRAP GRID OVERVIEW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Bootstrap grid system provides:

• 12-column layout

• Responsive breakpoints

• Containers

• Rows

• Columns

• Gutters

• Mobile-first behavior


GRID HIERARCHY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Container
   ↓
Row
   ↓
Columns
   ↓
Content


Example:

.container
   ↓
.row
   ↓
.col-md-4
.col-md-4
.col-md-4


Total:

4 + 4 + 4 = 12 columns


================================================================================
BOOTSTRAP BREAKPOINTS
================================================================================

+------------------+--------------+---------------------+
| BREAKPOINT       | PREFIX       | MINIMUM WIDTH       |
+------------------+--------------+---------------------+
| Extra Small      | none         | < 576px             |
| Small            | sm           | >= 576px            |
| Medium           | md           | >= 768px            |
| Large            | lg           | >= 992px            |
| Extra Large      | xl           | >= 1200px           |
| XXL              | xxl          | >= 1400px           |
+------------------+--------------+---------------------+


IMPORTANT:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bootstrap is mobile-first.

Example:

col-12 col-md-6 col-lg-3


means:

Small / Base:
12 columns = full row


Medium and above:
6 columns = half row


Large and above:
3 columns = quarter row


