PART 8: CUSTOMIZING BOOTSTRAP
================================================================================

METHOD 1: CUSTOM CSS OVERRIDES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bootstrap first:

import 'bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css'


Custom styles after:

import './index.css'


Example:

.btn-primary {
  background-color: #667eea;
  border-color: #667eea;
  font-weight: 600;
  border-radius: 8px;
}


.btn-primary:hover {
  background-color: #5568d3;
  border-color: #5568d3;
  transform:
    translateY(-2px);

  box-shadow:
    0 8px 16px
    rgba(102, 126, 234, 0.3);
}


.card {
  border: none;

  border-radius: 12px;

  box-shadow:
    0 4px 8px
    rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);

  transition:
    all 0.3s ease;
}


.card:hover {
  transform:
    translateY(-4px);

  box-shadow:
    0 8px 16px
    rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
}


.alert {
  border-radius: 8px;
  font-weight: 500;
}


================================================================================
METHOD 2: BOOTSTRAP CSS VARIABLES
================================================================================

Bootstrap exposes CSS custom properties for many runtime styling concerns.

You can override supported variables when appropriate.

Example:

:root {
  --bs-primary: #667eea;
  --bs-secondary: #764ba2;
}


IMPORTANT:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Do not assume that changing a single root variable automatically recompiles
every Bootstrap utility or variant exactly as Sass customization would.

Bootstrap's CSS variables and Bootstrap's Sass build-time customization are
related but different customization mechanisms.


================================================================================
METHOD 3: SASS CUSTOMIZATION
================================================================================

For deeper framework customization, Bootstrap's Sass source can be compiled
with custom variables/settings.

Conceptual flow:

Bootstrap Sass Source
        ↓
Custom Sass Variables
        ↓
Compile
        ↓
Customized Bootstrap CSS


================================================================================
CUSTOMIZATION OPTIONS
================================================================================

+----------------------+-----------------------------------------------+
| METHOD               | PURPOSE                                       |
+----------------------+-----------------------------------------------+
| Utility Classes      | Use existing Bootstrap design                 |
| Custom CSS           | Override/add project styles                   |
| CSS Variables        | Runtime-supported custom properties           |
| Sass                 | Deeper build-time customization               |
| Inline Style         | Dynamic element-specific value                |
| CSS Modules          | Scope your own component CSS                  |
| CSS-in-JS            | Alternative component styling approach        |
+----------------------+-----------------------------------------------+


IMPORTANT:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CSS Modules do NOT "scope Bootstrap itself."

They scope class names declared inside your own *.module.css files.


================================================================================
PART 9: BOOTSTRAP BEST PRACTICES
================================================================================

BEST PRACTICES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

• Use Semantic HTML
  - Bootstrap classes should enhance good HTML structure

• Use Grid When It Fits the Layout
  - container → row → columns

• Use Utilities for Common Styling
  - Spacing, alignment, colors, display, etc.

• Avoid Reimplementing Existing Bootstrap Styles Without a Reason

• Keep Custom CSS Focused
  - Add only application-specific styling

• Customize Intentionally
  - Avoid overriding large parts of Bootstrap unnecessarily

• Build Responsive Layouts
  - Use breakpoint-aware classes

• Test Accessibility
  - A Bootstrap class does not automatically make application logic accessible

• Include Bootstrap JS Only When Needed

• Prefer Bootstrap 5 Logical Spacing Utilities
  - ms / me / ps / pe

• Test on Different Screen Sizes

• Keep Framework Version in Mind
  - Classes/components can differ between Bootstrap releases


